alue":2019.05,"year":"2026-27","kind":"gbp"}]}},"dossier":{"summary":null,"compliance":{"score":130,"max":216,"pct":60,"assessed":"2026-02-26","notes":"Strongest area by a distance is the liability-benchmark work (LB-01/02/04 = 3): separate GF & HRA benchmarks built from the four balances, charted to ~2075 with a stated \u00a310m liquidity buffer - Arlingclose-quality and a genuine sector model. Core prudential indicators, MRP policy, reporting cycle, governance and creditworthiness (INV-03 = 3, uses CDS/other data beyond ratings) are all solid, and a genuinely strategic Capital Strategy (CS-01 = 3) is in place. Weakest areas are the commercial/non-treasury and interest-rate-risk disclosures: proportionality of commercial investment (COM-03, core) is a single sentence with no quantified capacity test; there is no fixed/variable interest-rate exposure indicator (RISK-02, core); and several statutory commercial/investment disclosures are thin or missing (COM-02 paras 51-53, COM-09 investment limits, PI-08 income ratio, INV-05 specified/non-specified, BOR-03 sterling-only, RPT-05 audit-qualification flag). Context: distressed unitary under statutory intervention with Commissioners and a Capitalisation Direction; strategy is tightly focused on debt reduction and refinancing an under-borrowed (internal-borrowing ~\u00a3200m) position as legacy loans run off.","gaps":[{"id":"PI-08","evidence":"p.21-22 Table 18 non-treasury interest receivable \u00a31.8m; p.20 s48.1 investment income \u00a31.3m; s49.3/s50.1 contribution to the budget"},{"id":"PI-10","evidence":"p.13 s23.5 / p.16 s29.1 holds no long-term (>364-day) treasury investments and does not envisage them; p.13 s24.1 investments beyond 365 days unlikely"},{"id":"COM-02","evidence":"TMSS p.6 s9.2 references the Prudential Code's prudent/not-prudent borrowing principles"},{"id":"COM-03","evidence":"TMSS p.23 s50.1 (commercial profit used to help achieve a balanced revenue budget); Capital Strategy p.10 'cautious' GF ri